---
// Cascade probe — VARIANT A (MEASURE-3, D-02 claim 3).
//
// Import shape: the design system's `tokens.css` FIRST, `theme-charcoal.css`
// SECOND, both in this frontmatter. Emitted order: tokens, then charcoal.
//
// The two lines below are the entire experiment. Astro decides the order of
// imported stylesheets with `cssOrder(a, b)` (astro/dist/core/build/runtime.js),
// which sorts by accumulated import index ascending then module-graph depth
// descending — and the import index is literally the position of the `import`
// statement inside the importing module. Swapping the two lines flips the
// emitted order every time, which is why this matrix is CONSTRUCTED rather
// than observed: you cannot reliably reproduce ordering nondeterminism by
// hoping to catch it, you reproduce it by building both orderings and
// asserting the theme wins in each.
//
// `data-brand="charcoal"` on <html> is what selects the theme. The `dark`
// class is deliberately ABSENT: `probe.mjs` toggles it on and off between
// reads so both modes are measured on one build of one page, and neither mode
// can be accidentally baked into the markup.
//
// Nothing else may differ between casc-a/b/c/d. Body, title and attributes are
// identical across all four by design — the import shape is the only variable.

import "@akhil-saxena/design-system/tokens.css";
import "../../styles/theme-charcoal.css";
---

<html lang="en" data-brand="charcoal">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>probe/casc-a — tokens then theme, both in .astro</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<h1>casc-a</h1>
		<p>tokens.css then theme-charcoal.css, both imported from .astro frontmatter.</p>
	</body>
</html>
